# Permissions

Owns the access vocabulary and enforcement model. Always enforce permission-based access; deny by default.

## Key Format

- Keys must be lowercase `resource:action` (snake_case), e.g. `clinical:write`, `rooms_beds:read`.
- Canonical catalog: `backend/src/config/permissions.js`; frontend must mirror it in `AppPermissions`.
- Shell entry uses one `*:read` key per menu destination (e.g. `opd:read`).
- New keys must land in both catalogs before seeds, gates, or APIs use them.

## Vocabulary

- Core actions: `read`, `write`, `update`, `delete`, `manage`, `export`, `approve`, `publish`, `admin`, `audit`.
- Module-specific actions may be added (`request`, `review`, `release`, `manage_storage`).
- Prefer `own` / `assigned` ABAC scope over manage-all grants.

## Access Model

- Authority order: subscription → assigned modules → roles/permissions → ABAC.
- Effective access = `union(role/module/user grants) ∩ subscription ∩ assigned modules ∩ ABAC`.
- Grants must not exceed the active package or actor ceiling.
- Users may hold multiple scoped roles via `user_role`.

## ABAC

- Scope covers tenant, facility, department, unit, ward, room, bed, ownership, assignment, shift, and status.
- Break-glass must be explicit, time-limited, and audited (`break_glass:*`).
- Every permission decision must be recordable and auditable.

## Enforcement

- UI, API, menu, route, component, and workflow access must pass effective-access checks.
- Backend is authoritative; UI hide/disable alone is never enough.
- Permission/role/module/subscription changes must be atomic, versioned, and auditable.
- Failed changes must roll back completely.

## Related Rules

- `modules.mdc`, `subscriptions.mdc`, `default_user_roles.mdc`
- `frontend/.cursor/permissions.mdc`, `backend/.cursor/auth-security.mdc`
